      "content": "For variable supplier lead times, consider using a safety stock formula that incorporates demand variability and lead time variability. A common approach is: Safety Stock = $Z \\times \\sqrt{(\\text{Average Lead Time} \\times \\text{Demand Variance}) + (\\text{Average Demand}^2 \\times \\text{Lead Time Variance})}$. This requires you to accurately track historical demand and lead time fluctuations to set the appropriate service level factor ($Z$). Remember that higher variability in either demand or lead time necessitates a higher buffer stock.",
